  "notes": "A tip-drive helicopter (PLAN Phase 5): the rotor shaft is FREE - no motor on it anywhere - and the head is driven entirely by two small propellers mounted at 92% radius on the blades, thrusting along the blades' direction of travel. Their torque enters the shaft as blade-frame force, never as shaft torque, so the airframe reaction is close to zero: NO TAIL ROTOR, and the hover test asserts the yaw barely drifts. The fin is for weathervaning in translation, not anti-torque.",
